e, sentence, and lexical diversity count. We’ll convert those lists and dictionaries into series and then put them into a dataframe. Finally, and to save the information, we’ll use a Pandas function to save that dataframe into a csv file. A comma-separated value file is an easy way to store table information in a text-only format.","position":{"start":{"line":41,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"key":"H9mhvm1EOU"}],"key":"plYKgWRZTj"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We start by importing all the packages we need. Note that we import Pandas as “pd”. That allows us to type the Pandas functions with a shorthand, “pd”, rather than the full “pandas”.","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"yAXcXDa1L2"}],"key":"EytoXZam3e"}],"key":"n6EMmSsoKO"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"import os\nimport nltk\nimport numpy\nimport matplotlib\nfrom nltk.tokenize import sent_tokenize, word_tokenize\nfrom nltk import FreqDist\nimport pandas as pd","key":"oh6FDqGvmc"},{"type":"outputs","id":"9-sytX18Olr_NktSMfFFM","children":[],"key":"ekqxuiNMRL"}],"key":"XrUlJH5XP7"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function definitions","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"E3vLdOcMsb"}],"identifier":"function-definitions","label":"Function definitions","html_id":"function-definitions","implicit":true,"key":"un7jO5Cutg"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We’ll reuse the functions from Week 4, with some modifications. The first one, ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"p6m3UJyr2Y"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get_text_info()","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"xUaTU7uAti"},{"type":"text","value":" now only calculates tokens and types. We’ll use the pandas dataframe to calculate the lexical diversity.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"yMtjoHf8XD"}],"key":"mTXVihXwti"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The second function is the same. It reads all the files in the directory and calculates the information from ","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"xI3Fep3YR4"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get_text_info","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"du7fpZ4IVm"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"Ool6nRiJyO"}],"key":"j8YqlpoRH2"}],"key":"WEd402sI21"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"def get_text_info(text):\n    \"\"\"\n    Uses NLTK to calculate: tokens, types, lexical diversity\n    \n    Args:\n        text (str): a string containing the file or text\n        \n    Returns: \n        dict: a dictionary containing tokens, types, and lexical diversity\n    \"\"\"\n    tokens = nltk.word_tokenize(text)\n    n_tokens = len(tokens)\n    n_types = len(set(tokens))\n    return {\n            'tokens': n_tokens,\n            'types': n_types,\n        }\n\n\ndef process_dir(path):\n    \"\"\"\n    Reads all the files in a directory. Processes them using the 'get_text_info' function\n    \n    Args: \n        path (str): path to the directory where the files are\n        \n    Returns:\n        dict: a dictionary with file names as keys and the tokens, types, lexical diversity, as values\n    \n    \"\"\"\n    file_info = {}\n\n    for filename in os.listdir(path):\n        if filename.endswith(\".txt\"):    \n            file_path = os.path.join(path, filename)      \n            with open(file_path, 'r', encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                text = f.read()\n                file_info[filename] = get_text_info(text)\n    return file_info","key":"vnBULnn5Or"},{"type":"outputs","id":"YKZn3VWveAY0Ed0qi120D","children":[],"key":"SlRIR9AkQu"}],"key":"E0vdycOh0d"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call the functions","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"mIEoPl8E36"}],"identifier":"call-the-functions","label":"Call the functions","html_id":"call-the-functions","implicit":true,"key":"KBFDbf2WEi"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":2,"column":1},"end":{"line":2,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We call the function ","position":{"start":{"line":2,"column":1},"end":{"line":2,"column":1}},"key":"AXhT5IN98x"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process_dir()","position":{"start":{"line":2,"column":1},"end":{"line":2,"column":1}},"key":"ccIVKfV4ZP"},{"type":"text","value":", which in turns calls ","position":{"start":{"line":2,"column":1},"end":{"line":2,"column":1}},"key":"jraU9mhQbQ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get_text_info()","position":{"start":{"line":2,"column":1},"end":{"line":2,"column":1}},"key":"Y4fxIYfxl8"},{"type":"text","value":" and returns a dictionary with the name of the file as key, and n_tokens and n_types for each file.","position":{"start":{"line":2,"column":1},"end":{"line":2,"column":1}},"key":"s4QlLi7ONV"}],"key":"v7ujihNw3b"}],"key":"NcpuWke5HC"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"# define the path. This directory should have more than 1 file\npath = './data'\n\nfiles_in_dir_info = pr